      "rationale": "L1 and L2 independently pin the exact junction: insert_after_residue=414 (G) / residue_after=415 (A), both within ECL4 (topology landmarks 395\u2013453). Python confirms residue 414 is G and residue 415 is A. The insertion site is 20 residues from the TM7 C-terminal boundary (394) and 39 residues from the TM8 N-terminal boundary (454), well beyond the \u22653-residue minimum. Although C416 and C421 are nearby, the published experiments demonstrate the tag is tolerated and the protein reaches the cell surface, overriding any structural concern. L1 (PMC10030352) and L2 (PMC12365235) both explicitly report insertion of an HA epitope flanked by SGSGG linkers between residues 414 and 415 of full-length, membrane-anchored human NCC (SLC12A3) in extracellular loop 4. L3 (same paper as L1) confirms surface display by anti-HA staining of non-permeabilized cells.",
